{{!-- Faith Received — the Bookmarks workspace.

     Every work the reader has saved from the library, most recent
     first, each one a link back into the reader and each one removable
     from here. Bound by assets/js/page/faith-bookmarks.js — read that
     file's header for where bookmarks actually live (the mo-kit
     Worker's KV, not localStorage and not Ghost) and for how a reader
     link is built.

     SELF-CONTAINED. Unlike _ask-panel.hbs, this partial ships its own
     <script> tags at the bottom. It is written to be dropped into a
     workspace shell (the Research page's Bookmarks tab) whose template
     is owned by someone else, and a partial whose host has to remember
     to add two script tags is a partial that renders a permanent
     "Loading…" the first time anyone reuses it. The same pattern is
     already in partials/faith-received/_topics-index.hbs and
     partials/membership-body.hbs.

     A host page that ALSO loads js/faith-corpora.js or
     js/page/faith-bookmarks.js is harmless: faith-corpora.js only
     redefines window.MOCorpora, and faith-bookmarks.js binds once and
     returns on a second run (it marks [data-fb-root] with
     data-fb-bound). It does NOT need feature-gate.js: nothing here
     calls an LLM or costs money, and the panel gates itself on
     data-member-status because the bookmark store is per member.

     DOM contract faith-bookmarks.js depends on — re-read that file
     before touching any of this:
       - [data-fb-root] wrapping everything. The script marks it bound
         and hangs the click / focusout handlers that cancel a pending
         Remove on it.
       - [data-fb-status] — the one status line. Three states, three
         different renders: loading, error, and the ordinary empty
         panel. An empty state is a claim and a failed fetch is not
         allowed to make it, so "nothing saved" is painted into
         [data-fb-list] only after a read that succeeded.
       - [data-fb-count] — the running total, hidden until there is one.
       - [data-fb-sort] holding three button[data-fb-sort-by] with the
         values "recent", "author" and "collection". Hidden by the
         script below two saved works. "recent" is the default AND is
         the order the worker returns; nothing may re-sort it in place.
       - [data-fb-list] — everything rendered. Rows carry [data-fb-id]
         (the full "tfr:<corpus>:<work>" bookmark id) and a
         button[data-fb-remove]; the error state carries
         button[data-fb-retry].

     Rendered on its own page rather than in a tab strip, wrap it in a
     <section class="bband"> and give the page its own hero. Nothing in
     here depends on the tab shell. --}}
<div class="bookmarks-workspace" data-fb-root>
  <div class="bookmarks-workspace-inner">

    <header class="bookmarks-head">
      <div class="bookmarks-head-text">
        <h2 class="bookmarks-title">Bookmarks</h2>
        <p class="bookmarks-count" data-fb-count hidden></p>
      </div>

      {{!-- Sort. Plain text toggles on a hairline, not a select and not
            a row of pills: this is apparatus, and the panel below it is
            the thing being looked at. Hidden by the script until there
            are at least two works to order. --}}
      <div class="bookmarks-sort" data-fb-sort role="group" aria-label="Order saved works" hidden>
        <button type="button" class="bookmarks-sort-btn is-active" data-fb-sort-by="recent" aria-pressed="true">Recent</button>
        <button type="button" class="bookmarks-sort-btn" data-fb-sort-by="author" aria-pressed="false">Author</button>
        <button type="button" class="bookmarks-sort-btn" data-fb-sort-by="collection" aria-pressed="false">Collection</button>
      </div>
    </header>

    <p class="bookmarks-status" data-fb-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading your saved works&hellip;</p>

    <div class="bookmarks-list" data-fb-list></div>

  </div>
</div>

{{!-- Last inside the panel on purpose: a non-visual node placed first
      would take the :first-child margin reset off the header above it.
      faith-corpora.js first — faith-bookmarks.js resolves saved ids
      against window.MOCorpora, and page-template scripts run before
      site.min.js, so nothing bundled can be assumed here. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-corpora.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-bookmarks.js"}}"></script>
